# Known-historical findings only — the current tree is clean (verified
# 2026-08-29, see docker/Dockerfile.web and the app/docs/** pages below).
# `gitleaks detect` walks every commit in history, so an already-pushed
# commit keeps tripping a rule forever even after the next commit fixes it
# forward — baselining here is this repo's chosen fix, matching the
# convention already established in jitterflow-core-app's own
# .gitleaksignore. Never add a fingerprint for a CURRENT file here — fix
# the leak instead.
#
# All 26 below are commit 3bddb31441e509d59ca9c8870a4ea3abf2650674 (already
# on origin/main by the time this was caught), the commit that added the
# /docs section. Re-derive with `gitleaks detect --source . --redact
# --report-format json` if this ever needs doing again — matches by
# file+rule+line, commit SHA is the only part that moves.

# Not a real secret — docker/Dockerfile.web's own build-time ARG default
# (never read by `next build`, see that file's comment) used to be literally
# named "sk_test_placeholder", which is real-Stripe-key-shaped enough to
# match gitleaks'/trivy's stripe-access-token regex. Fixed forward in the
# current tree to a value with no sk_test_/sk_live_ prefix at all.
3bddb31441e509d59ca9c8870a4ea3abf2650674:docker/Dockerfile.web:stripe-access-token:27

